{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('state.json'))\nfor q in d['investigations']:\n    if q['id']=='b4ce39b510974e628f7333fe0525a25b-question-0':\n        print(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in q.items() if k\"'!='\"'latest_interpretation'},indent=1)[:4000])\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"id\": \"b4ce39b510974e628f7333fe0525a25b-question-0\",\n \"version\": 18,\n \"question\": \"Can a follower that holds an accepted StopSign be left behind, with its decided index stuck at the StopSign's position, when the current leader's decided index has advanced beyond its own log and the leader's Decides are the follower's next expected sequence messages?\",\n \"source_ids\": [\n  \"core_resend_leader\",\n  \"core_send_decide\",\n  \"core_update_decided_clamp\",\n  \"core_stopsign_decided\",\n  \"core_handle_acceptsync\",\n  \"core_send_accsync\"\n ],\n \"hypothesis\": \"An AcceptSync whose prefix already covers the StopSign but which also carries it makes sync_log add one to the accepted index without placing an entry, so the accepted index lands one past the readable log, the marker is relocated to the inflated position and the StopSign loses its decided status because decided no longer equals accepted. In the randomized run the same shape arises at scale: the inflated accepted index lets a shorter group's leader decide an index no local log supports, and the stalled follower's sequence-expected Decides clamp its decided index instead of reconnecting.\",\n \"discriminator\": \"\",\n \"disposition\": \"explained\",\n \"parent_id\": null,\n \"knowledge\": [\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"5162a11f32d548bdbd346a1de302af4d-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"Control for the covering witness: sync_idx 2 with the same StopSign-carrying payload leaves accepted 3, decided 3, is_reconfigured Some and the marker at index 2, so the inflation is specific to a prefix that already covers the marker.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"dc8a6ab507df45f885e3843d5863a22e-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"The contrasting covering case: sync_idx 3 raises accepted to 4, moves the marker to index 3 and clears its decided status.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"09dbcecc828c48239e683c97347101cf-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"The source arithmetic that distinguishes the two cases: the extra one is added for the StopSign on top of whatever the prefix already covers.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"0d2824065dd745ca9d3bda4294bf56c7-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"The randomized run shows the same distinction at scale: accepted reached 38 before any marker was present, and the marker later filled the last counted slot.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"resume_conditions\": [],\n \"gaps\": [],\n \"history\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"b4ce39b510974e628f7333fe0525a25b-question-0\",\n   \"version\": 1,\n   \"question\": \"Can a follower that promised a stable leader but missed the AcceptStopSign recover after that StopSign becomes decided, or is it stuck behind with decided < accepted-by-others and no enabled repair?\",\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"core_resend_leader\",\n    \"core_send_decide\",\n    \"core_update_decided_clamp\",\n    \"core_stopsign_decided\",\n    \"core_handle_acceptsync\",\n    \"core_send_accsync\"\n   ],\n   \"hypothesis\": \"It is stuck. resend_messages_leader resends the StopSign Decide once stopsign_is_decided and resends AcceptStopSign only while the StopSign is undecided. send_decide resends with the last used sequence number, and even an accepted Decide cannot advance a follower whose accepted index is below the decision: update_decided_idx_and_get_accepted_idx clamps decided to the flushed accepted index, so the follower stays at its old decided value. AcceptSync, which would carry the missing StopSign and the leader's decided index, is sent only in response to a Promise, and a stable leader sends Prepare only to peers that are not promised. The follower therefore makes no progress until leadership changes or the user reconnects it.\",\n   \"discriminator\": \"The lagging follower's accepted index, decided index, leader view, phase and promise ballot after many fair-delivery rounds that exceed the resend timeout, together with the source paths that decide which repair message is sent in each StopSign state.\",\n   \"disposition\": \"active\",\n   \"parent_id\": null,\n   \"knowledge\": [],\n   \"resume_conditions\": [],\n   \"operation_id\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
